//youtu.be/-zWq54D4Pk8", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Graham Platners Chosen Succsessor At Desecration Of Civi War Memorial And Sing Along For The Murder Of A Sitting President", "last_comment_created": 1786284279783, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 13, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCE208Xq", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 14, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8771332, "raw_content": "This study revealed that, overall, the slaughter method had limited influence on the sensory and textural properties of beef. Our results revealed no significant differences for sensory evaluation (odour and flavour) and textural properties between halal with and without stunning and conventional slaughters, excepting urine and milk odours, metallic flavour, and a trend toward significance for red and yellow indices only for the Transversus abdominis muscle. For this muscle, beef samples from halal-acceptable stunning (HAS) demonstrated lower scores for undesirable odours and metallic flavour and tended to show lower red and yellow indices than samples from nonstunning halal slaughter (NHS) and conventional slaughter (CONV). The type of slaughter did not affect liver or blood odours/flavours, nor the water-holding capacity measured from the cooking losses.\n\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12070996/", "author": "cyberrigger", "created": 1786282582187, "profile_picture": "0UVsiKsLavnh", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "BrockingmySampson", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Influence of Halal Slaughter on the Colour, Odour, Flavour, and Textural Properties of Beef ---- no difference", "last_comment_created": 1786288178821, "content": "<p>This study revealed that, overall, the slaughter method had limited influence on the sensory and textural properties of beef. Our results revealed no significant differences for sensory evaluation (odour and flavour) and textural properties between halal with and without stunning and conventional slaughters, excepting urine and milk odours, metallic flavour, and a trend toward significance for red and yellow indices only for the Transversus abdominis muscle. For this muscle, beef samples from halal-acceptable stunning (HAS) demonstrated lower scores for undesirable odours and metallic flavour and tended to show lower red and yellow indices than samples from nonstunning halal slaughter (NHS) and conventional slaughter (CONV). The type of slaughter did not affect liver or blood odours/flavours, nor the water-holding capacity measured from the cooking losses.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12070996/\" target=\"_blank\">https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12070996/</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 13, "score_up": 14, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCE1zaqY", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_f